 "description": "<p>In June 28, 2021, Group-IB Managed XDR detected a malicious spearphishing email. As you can see our solution quickly blocked the malicious email.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/2689348f01ad5a01e9353015993fb481b37410f647ffb9ce361d46420dc61069?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:2689348f01ad5a01e9353015993fb481b37410f647ffb9ce361d46420dc61069_IMAGE__\" data-mce-src=\"__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:2689348f01ad5a01e9353015993fb481b37410f647ffb9ce361d46420dc61069_IMAGE__\" /></figure><p>Inside of this email was a malicious file, which we detected and have verdict - malicious:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/44a1403cc37e427e9fe9cc0be0ec89dadc903e77f5baa5b6a0b36052286f8646?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:44a1403cc37e427e9fe9cc0be0ec89dadc903e77f5baa5b6a0b36052286f8646_IMAGE__\" data-mce-src=\"__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:44a1403cc37e427e9fe9cc0be0ec89dadc903e77f5baa5b6a0b36052286f8646_IMAGE__\" /></figure><p>A malicious file from email attachment analysis report in our sandbox (Polygon):</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/b681f863606e601b39d066798a2ce43f6c93d09fd82177d2c6be3b60f378547b?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:b681f863606e601b39d066798a2ce43f6c93d09fd82177d2c6be3b60f378547b_IMAGE__\" data-mce-src=\"__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:b681f863606e601b39d066798a2ce43f6c93d09fd82177d2c6be3b60f378547b_IMAGE__\" /></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>Initial vector</h2><p>The attacker uses mail as an initial vector of compromise. The file \"30 июня в 17.30 - очередное заседание Исполкома АДЭ.doc\" is attached to an email message.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/8587a4ace090e49b907c6edeae641f0d5f57adadb4199f4126cab9ee8a9af494?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:8587a4ace090e49b907c6edeae641f0d5f57adadb4199f4126cab9ee8a9af494_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><h2>RoyalRoad RTF</h2><p>The analyzed file \"30 июня в 17.30 - очередное заседание Исполкома АДЭ.doc\" (this file is private, it's not uploaded on VT) is a malicious RTF document which was weaponized by Royal Road RTF Weaponizer. Royal Road is commonly used by Chinese-speaking attackers.<br>The decoy is about the next meeting of the Executive Committee of the Documentary Telecommunications Association:</p><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"width:385px;\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/1076d94346a1427d8d9f3bad62f263b1c97915bafb55a9fb21ca9a6b10a249e2?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:1076d94346a1427d8d9f3bad62f263b1c97915bafb55a9fb21ca9a6b10a249e2_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Meta-information:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/ee28d2eb1c95879a2fcfa55c95115b9664775385800b750991cea022b466608e?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:ee28d2eb1c95879a2fcfa55c95115b9664775385800b750991cea022b466608e_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><p>The malicious encoded payload:<br>&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/97b95f3a16e23b85e788438654706109e346a14fbeb0d2e35ad90ae5513f7de3?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:97b95f3a16e23b85e788438654706109e346a14fbeb0d2e35ad90ae5513f7de3_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><h2>Decoded payload - Bisonal.Dropper</h2><p>The decoded payload is a malicious PE32 format DLL file which can be classified as Bisonal.Dropper. This malware is used to deploy in a victim system a Bisonal backdoor.<br>Compilation TimeDateStamp: 28.06.2021 01:44:01 UTC The Bisonal.Dropper creates a file \"%AppData%\\Roaming\\conhost.exe\" (Bisonal.DoubleT backdoor). It writes a random overlay data to \"conhost.exe\" to change the hash of a backdoor.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/ab35433efb99d0f95b41cc2c2fc6d1792cdff0f65740f12134d424c45400480d?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:ab35433efb99d0f95b41cc2c2fc6d1792cdff0f65740f12134d424c45400480d_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/80beda2972343a3a398d354c32b94b25bedac006657437c3a15958a65f96804b?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:80beda2972343a3a398d354c32b94b25bedac006657437c3a15958a65f96804b_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><p>The dropper also adds \"conhost.exe\" to a system startup by creating a registry key parameter:</p><pre><code class=\"language-plaintext\">[HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run] userInit = \"%AppData%\\Roaming\\conhost.exe\"</code></pre><p>The backdoor will only run after the system reboot.<br>Also it can write to the log file \"%windows%\\temp\\log.txt\" following error messages:</p><ul><li>\"[!] get pRegSetValueEx error\\n\"</li><li>\"[!] get pGetProcAddress error\\n\"</li><li>\"[!] get LoadLibraryA error\\n\"</li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/34124b8f09ca9df144f5facdd19cc5b45200781c91efc68e9776ab209a16d918?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:34124b8f09ca9df144f5facdd19cc5b45200781c91efc68e9776ab209a16d918_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><h2>Bisonal.DoubleT variant</h2><p>\"conhost.exe\" is a malicious PE32 format EXE file which can be classified as a Bisonal.DoubleT backdoor. This malware provides remote access to a compromised computer and allows an attacker to execute various commands on it.<br>Compilation TimeDateStamp: 24.06.2021 07:19:44 UTC<br>Main functionality (capabilities):</p><ul><li>collect information about compromised host: code page layout, proxy server, time since system boot, host name, account name under which the file is running, local IP address;</li><li>get a list of processes;</li><li>terminate a specified process;</li><li>get remote access to cmd.exe;</li><li>download and execute file;</li><li>get code page identifier and write file (create file on disk).</li></ul><p>The collected information about compromised host is encoded with Base32 algorithm.<br>All important strings are encrypted with following RC4 (S-box 128) algorithm:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/a4ee24275d901d27ac6b31f344b321084b243c9eaf888306f86eb8c2e2196d81?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:a4ee24275d901d27ac6b31f344b321084b243c9eaf888306f86eb8c2e2196d81_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><p>After decryption strings looks like this:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e/file/43a2606936e30f6938dd11a435925064acbdb793ee4196c099af877990018807?placeholder=__IMAGE_db7376043e44cb710fb1faeaa3d4b34e2e961e1e:43a2606936e30f6938dd11a435925064acbdb793ee4196c099af877990018807_IMAGE__\"  /></figure><p>The transmitted data in POST request (sending the result of the command execution) is encrypted with the same algorithm as the strings in the body of the malware.</p><h2>Additional IOCs</h2><h3>URLs</h3><ul><li>(Hello - GET request) hXXps://103[.]85[.]20[.]194/ru/order/index.php?strPageID=[ID], where ID is a decimal number (example: hXXps://103[.]85[.]20[.]194/ru/order/index.php?strPageID=0)</li><li>(Command - GET request) hXXps://103[.]85[.]20[.]194/ru/news/index.php?strPageID=[ID]&amp;newsID=[YYYY-MM-DD-mmss]</li><li>(Response- POST request) hXXps://103[.]85[.]20[.]194/xhome[.]native[.]page/datareader.php?sid=[ID]</li><li>(Download &amp; Execute - GET request) hXXps://103[.]85[.]20[.]194/siteFiles/index.php?strPageID=[ID]</li></ul><h3>Files</h3><ul><li>%AppData%\\Roaming\\conhost.exe</li><li>%Windows%\\temp\\log.txt</li></ul><h3>Registry</h3><p>[HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run] userInit =\"%AppData%\\Roaming\\conhost.exe\"</p><h3>User-Agent</h3><pre><code class=\"language-plaintext\">User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.181 Safari/537.36\\r\\nAccept-Encoding: gzip, deflate\\r\\nAccept-Language: ru-RU,ru;q=0.9,en-US;q=0.8,en;q=0.7\\r\\nCookie: JSESSIONID=[Base32 encoded information about victim computer]</code></pre>",
